-- Young Offenders Act 1994 (WA), ss 3, 4, 14, 22-33, 37A, 40, 41, 55, 62, 71, 189, 190 -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case or subsidiary legislation (none was retrieved).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_wa_young-offenders-act-1994_baseline.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

-- Life facts are from the workbench scenario au/wa/cradle-to-grave-jake/facts.json (Jake born 30 August 2006). The
-- scenario does not say who attended the team; the fixture ASSUMES his mother and the store manager attended and agreed.
-- Plain stealing (The Criminal Code s 378) is in neither Schedule; Schedule 2 lists only s 378(2) (motor vehicle,
-- aggravated) and s 392 (robbery) among the stealing offences.

