§ `ss 3, 4 -- am I a young person (k022 at 15; k082 at 40)`

#ASSERT `Am I a young person for this offence` (Date 30 8 2006) (Date 20 11 2021)
#ASSERT NOT `Am I a young person for this offence` (Date 30 8 2006) (Date 30 8 2024)

#ASSERT `age in completed years` (Date 30 8 2006) (Date 4 3 2047) EQUALS 40

-- k082: at 40 he is still a young person for the 2021 offence (s 4): the test is his age on the day of the offence.
#ASSERT `I am a young person for it` `Jake's shop theft, 20 November 2021`

#ASSERT NOT `Am I an independent young person` (Date 30 8 2006) (Date 14 2 2022) TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I an independent young person` (Date 1 1 2005) (Date 14 2 2022) TRUE

§ `ss 22B, 41 -- what police must consider and may do (k022)`

#ASSERT `Must police consider no action or a caution before charging me` `Jake's shop theft, 20 November 2021`
#ASSERT `Must police consider no action or a caution before charging me` `a robbery (Schedule 2)`
#ASSERT NOT `Must police consider no action or a caution before charging me` `the same theft on his 18th birthday`

#ASSERT `Is this option open to police` `give me a caution` `Jake's shop theft, 20 November 2021`
#ASSERT `Is this option open to police` `refer me to a juvenile justice team` `Jake's shop theft, 20 November 2021`
#ASSERT NOT `Is this option open to police` `give me a caution` `a robbery (Schedule 2)`
#ASSERT NOT `Is this option open to police` `charge me without taking me into custody` `a matter without enough evidence to charge`

§ `ss 22, 23, 23A -- cautions (k022)`

#ASSERT `May police caution me instead of charging me` `Jake's shop theft, 20 November 2021`
#ASSERT NOT `May police caution me instead of charging me` `aiding suicide (Schedule 1)`
#ASSERT NOT `May police caution me instead of charging me` `a Weapons Act s 6(1) offence`
#ASSERT NOT `May police caution me instead of charging me` `the same theft on his 18th birthday`
#ASSERT NOT `May police caution me instead of charging me` `a matter without enough evidence to charge`

-- k022: the scenario's reason (a second offence the same night) is not s 23's test, which looks back to offences charged
-- or dealt with under Part 5. On Jake's facts the Act still prefers a caution to a charge.
#ASSERT `Should police caution me rather than charge me` `Jake's shop theft, 20 November 2021`
#ASSERT NOT `Should police caution me rather than charge me` `a theft after earlier charged offences`

#ASSERT `Must I be given a caution certificate` TRUE

#ASSERT NOT `Can what I said be used as evidence against me` `an admission at or about the time of my caution`
#ASSERT NOT `Can what I said be used as evidence against me` `my acceptance of responsibility to go to a team`

