-- k036 (five years on) and k082 (the job form at 40): the team left no conviction, so this Act gives him nothing to spend
-- or disclose. Whether the form's question reaches a team matter is the form's words and the Spent Convictions Act 1988.
#ASSERT `Is there a conviction from my matter to spend` `a juvenile justice team, terms completed` `no conviction` (Date 20 11 2026) EQUALS `nothing: no conviction was recorded`
#ASSERT `Is there a conviction from my matter to spend` `a juvenile justice team, terms completed` `no conviction` (Date 4 3 2047) EQUALS `nothing: no conviction was recorded`
#ASSERT `Is there a conviction from my matter to spend` `a finding of guilt with a conviction recorded` `a conviction with detention discharged 1 December 2022` (Date 1 12 2024) EQUALS `a conviction that no longer counts, treated as spent under the Spent Convictions Act Part 3`
#ASSERT `Is there a conviction from my matter to spend` `a finding of guilt with a conviction recorded` `a conviction with detention discharged 1 December 2022` (Date 30 11 2024) EQUALS `a conviction that still counts`

